# 2x 5060 Ti + 2x 3090 as PP2 x TP2 (John 10-31: swap two 3090s for two 5060 Tis). FUNCTIONAL test only:
# 80 GiB VRAM < ~75 GiB weights + KV + graphs, so experts must spill to RAM (prefill takes the staged path).
# Stage 0 = the two 5060 Tis (fewer layers: ~half the bandwidth), stage 1 = the two 3090s (lm_head + MTP).
# FILL IN the CUDA indices after the swap: `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=index,name,pci.bus_id --format=csv`
# (PCI bus order, matching CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID); list the 5060 Tis FIRST.
PP_GRAFTS=1
PP_SIZE=2
TP_SIZE=2
CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=__5060A__,__5060B__,__3090A__,__3090B__
VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION=18,30
# --cpu-offload-gb is per GPU (same on every rank); 7 GiB/card frees the 3090 stage, the 5060 Tis get extra room.
CPU_OFFLOAD_GB=7
KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES=1900000000
KV_TIER_DIR=/home/ai-host/models/kv-tier-pp-mixed
JIT_CACHE_DIR=./jit-cache-pp-mixed
